# Research and competitive analysis — not for the public repo
context/
rfps.md
# `docs/*` rather than `docs/`, so a single file can be un-excluded below. Git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation under a plain `docs/` would never fire.
docs/*
# The operator-facing deployment topology (story 1.6 / AD-17). It SHIPS: it is the doc that
# gives every process a named host, every relayer job its degrade state, and the cold-start
# caveat somewhere an operator or a reviewer will actually meet it — which is the whole point
# of writing it. It is neither research nor competitive analysis, so the rule above does not
# describe it. Everything else under docs/ (the retired Superpowers plans) stays excluded.
!docs/topology.md
# The user-facing privacy page (story 6.7 / FR-058). It ships for the same reason.
!docs/privacy.md
# The governance spec (walk 3, RFP IDEA-27). It ships with the branch so the merge back to main
# carries the architecture the managers argue with; same reasoning as topology above.
!docs/governance.md
# The maintained authenticated-app implementation ledger. Dated handoffs stay historical; this
# file is the normal repository source for shipped, retained, deployment-blocked and scoped-out work.
!docs/studio-rebuild-status.md

# Upstream sources cloned for ground truth — not ours to ship
reference/
.vercel
.env*
# The router plugin's scratch directory. It writes a uniquely-named temp file on every codegen run,
# so left tracked it adds one junk file per build to every commit.
apps/web/.tanstack/

# UNSPENT BEARER SECRETS, AND THIS IS A SECURITY LINE RATHER THAN A TIDINESS ONE.
#
# A position secret IS the money: `poseidon(secret)` is the commitment, and the contracts pay
# whoever presents the preimage — no address is checked, because not checking one is the entire
# point. So a live secret in a public repository is a public claim on the position, and this
# repository is going public.
#
# `evidence/` keeps the SPENT ones on purpose: once a position is CLAIMED the preimage buys nothing,
# and leaving it in lets any reader hash it themselves and watch the commitment fall out — the
# scheme demonstrated rather than asserted. Anything still claimable lives here instead, and
# `evidence/` points at it by name.
.secrets/
